	    failure state cannot be a panel invented on one screen.

	    THE SECOND SENTENCE IS THE ARTEFACT. "The originals are still staged.
	    Retrying does not re-upload them." D-15 requires the failure to be
	    RECOVERABLE by retrying the dispatch without re-uploading, and the
	    difference between a retry a user trusts and one they fear is entirely
	    whether the screen says so. An operator who thinks retry means re-upload
	    will not press it on a slow connection, and the two photos stay stuck.

	    G-8 is why the strip is in the topbar at all: AppShell's slots are
	    sidebar / topbar / main / footer, with no banner region. */}
	{o === "pipeline-failure" && (
		<div class="ov-treatment" data-artefact="O-pipeline-strip">
			<Eyebrow size="sm" tone="muted">PIPELINE FAILURE (D-15) — THE STRIP IS ABOVE</Eyebrow>
			<Heading level={2} size="lg" weight="bold">{PIPE_TITLE}</Heading>
			<Text size="sm" tone="muted">{PIPE_BODY}</Text>
			<div class="ov-actions">
